config BR2_PACKAGE_PYTHON_RNS_TIME
	bool "python-rns-time"
	select BR2_PACKAGE_PYTHON_RNS  # runtime
	help
	  rns-time — authenticated time over Reticulum.

	  The server asks ordinary NTP servers for the time and serves the
	  corrected time over Reticulum protocol v1 (app "rnstime", aspect
	  "time"). It needs no chrony, no GPS and no root: the measured
	  offset is added to the timestamps it hands out, so a host whose
	  own clock is wrong still serves correct time. It runs next to
	  rnsd through the shared instance.

	  The client measures time and --apply is used by
	  /etc/init.d/S88rnstime to set the box clock from a mesh time
	  server when ordinary NTP is unreachable. MeshAPI clients can
	  also use the "now" op.

	  https://github.com/wdunn001/rns-time
